commit 55b1810ae966a7a39c0066d8c9149015d232a4c3
Author: Jacob Chapel <jacob.chapel@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Mar 6 22:25:58 2026 -0800

    fix(web-ui): fix triage and inbox page dropdown filters not functioning

    The filter dropdowns used `bind:value` (two-way binding) combined with
    `$effect` syncing from URL params, creating a conflict: bind:value would
    set state immediately, but the $effect reading stale URL params could
    reset it back before goto() completed.

    Fix by deriving filter state directly from URL search params using
    `$derived`/$derived.by` (matching the working TaskFilters pattern),
    and switching selects from `bind:value` to one-way `value` attribute.
    URL params are now the single source of truth for filter state.

    Task: @01KK2T53XATPSTVMRNGCHCX23W
    Spec: @interactive-triage

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

